cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Risk-Adjusted Abstention for Root Cause Analysis"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered study of risk-sensitive selective prediction for
  LLM-assisted root cause analysis in Kubernetes. Derives a per-incident
  abstention threshold from SLO error-budget burn, infrastructure cost and
  blast radius, all estimated from telemetry rather than business-cost labels,
  and proves the threshold's dependence on incident stake changes sign at an
  interpretable boundary. Evaluated on two independent AIOps benchmarks
  (RCAEval RE1 and RCA100, 352 labelled failures), the hypothesis is refuted:
  the derived threshold loses to a hindsight-tuned constant on both corpora,
  and the sign of the result is set by an exchange rate no telemetry supplies.
authors:
